Found a second per-tick scaling issue in `VolcanicHeatSourceIndex.expire`: it copied `sources.values()` every Overworld tick, potentially touching the full ~16.7k source capacity just to remove at most 32 expired dynamic sources.

Correction:
- temporary heat sources are indexed by expiry deadline (`deadline -> UUIDs` plus reverse UUID mapping);
- permanent `Long.MAX_VALUE` geothermal sources are not scheduled for expiry at all;
- source replacement removes the previous deadline before scheduling the new one;
- explicit removal clears spatial and expiry membership together;
- `expire(gameTick, maxRemovals)` now visits only due deadline entries and remains bounded by `maxRemovals`;
- tests assert permanent sources are excluded from expiry scheduling and replacement does not leave stale deadlines.

