Stage-07 cross-stage capacity note — H07-023

Stage 04 integration now exposes `AtmosphericSourceSink.tryUpsert(...) -> AtmosphericSourceAdmission`; ordinary new-source saturation returns `REJECTED_CAPACITY` without mutating the Atmosphere index/lifecycle, while same-UUID replacement remains transactional at full capacity.

`GeothermalSourceRegistry` correctly remains persistent authority and its `GeothermalSourceLifecycleSink` is deliberately void/fail-isolated, so a future Atmosphere observer cannot communicate capacity pressure by throwing — that exception would be swallowed and the projection could disappear silently.

Stage 07 therefore specified the final bridge contract in `plans/07-hardening/evidence/atmosphere-external-admission-retry-contract.md` at Stage-07 commit `182013e5d2288402475fbfa5f01da1096d83297e`:
- at most one pending Atmosphere projection per authoritative UUID;
- latest upstream upsert replaces the pending payload (latest-wins, no duplicate queue entries);
- finite deterministic global retry capacity and attempts-per-tick budget;
- `remove(UUID)` cancels pending work before active projection removal so stale retry cannot resurrect a deleted source;
- successful admission clears pending state;
- restart reconstruction comes from complete authoritative Stage-03 registry replay, not a second Atmosphere SavedData authority;
- mixed ash + geothermal retry state must have a proven finite aggregate bound.

No geothermal core change is requested before the owning cross-stage RED can execute. This is the required handoff shape once Stage 03 and Stage 04 are canonical together.

