Current `AtmosphereSavedData` already has useful UUID-sorted serialization and per-entry malformed-source isolation, but the final release contract additionally requires:
- top-level schema v1 over the real current unversioned payload (v0);
- v0 -> v1 normalization;
- conflicting duplicate UUIDs must not be list-order last-wins: preserve the first accepted valid authority and skip/log the conflicting later entry;
- future/unknown schema payload preservation with read-only downgrade protection;
- no EXTERNAL source persistence; those remain upstream replay + H07-023 bounded admission/retry.

No production change requested until the integration branch is refreshed onto current main and the owner RED can execute.

Refinement to the previous global-budget note: do **not** let transient PENDING always consume all 16 before recovery, because sustained generation could starve durable crash recovery. Fair hard-budget policy should be:

- only transient work: up to 16 attempts;
- only recovery work: up to 2 chunks × max 8 receipts;
- both present: reserve one recovery unit, so transient gets at most 8 attempts and recovery gets 1 loaded chunk (≤8 receipts).

This guarantees progress for both authorities while preserving the same hard 16-item/tick envelope. The queue will need a bounded-attempt processing API/result (attempted count, not only acknowledged count), because negative acknowledgements/exceptions still consume server work and must count against the turn budget.

Stage-07 hardening blocker on HEAD `a298fff2aee44406dddb001a4863ecbcb7eb32ac`: this branch currently regresses two already-established MineColonies safety invariants and must not supersede/merge over PR #34 as-is.

**1. ABSENT-host semantics are wrong.** `MineColoniesCompat.serviceIfCompatible(false, ...)` returns `ProtectedAreaService.empty()`, whose `allowsTerrainMutation()` is false. `OptionalIntegrationBootstrap.install()` always installs that service into `VolcanicHazardWorldRuntime`, and the current test explicitly expects absent MineColonies to deny mutation. Standalone Volcanoes must instead treat an absent optional claim system as a valid **authoritative zero-provider** state so ordinary volcanic terrain effects remain available. Only PRESENT-but-unresolved/incompatible host state should fail closed/non-authoritative.

**2. Exact-version gating was dropped.** This branch says the distributed runtime version is not independently proven and gates only on `ModList.isLoaded("minecolonies")`. Stage-07/PR #34 already traced the upstream release/resource-processing pipeline and established the runtime metadata for the audited artifact/tag as exactly `1.1.1374-1.21.1-snapshot`. A merely present wrong-version host that still links far enough to construct the provider must not establish destructive mutation authority. Preserve an exact verified-version gate before optional MineColonies class resolution; wrong-version => non-authoritative fail-closed.

Required TDD contracts before this blocker is removed:
- ABSENT => authoritative zero-provider and provider factory is not resolved;
- PRESENT exact version + compatible API => authoritative provider;
- PRESENT wrong version => provider factory is not resolved and service is non-authoritative;
- PRESENT exact version with construction/runtime/linkage failure => fail closed;
- keep the `getClaimData(ResourceKey<Level>, ChunkPos)` no-force-load lookup.

Do not merge PR #34 first and then mechanically layer this weaker implementation. Port the stronger semantics into the canonical Stage-06 branch; supersede #34 only after semantic equivalence is proven and exact-head CI executes GREEN.

Stage-07 review of current Pressure integration HEAD `5ee7d9f8c290b559954e490cd7b2327e6a14b1ea`: H07-024 is structurally mitigated in `AtmosphericPressureResolver`. Selected optional-provider exception/linkage/null/malformed numeric output now falls directly to the validated built-in model without consulting lower external providers; invalid built-in output remains a strict core/config error.

Remaining focused acceptance before H07-024 can be removed / this part of the merge gate considered complete:
1. add or retain an explicit `Double.NEGATIVE_INFINITY` external-provider case (positive infinity, NaN and finite negative are already covered);
2. add a coordinator/player-tick-level contract proving malformed optional output cannot escape the owning tick and still yields a finite deterministic `PressureEntityUpdate`;
3. exact current HEAD must execute the full Pressure pipeline GREEN (unit → diff sanity → build → JAR → combined Eruption/Pressure GameTests → dedicated-server smoke).

No broad catch around the whole player tick is requested; keep the narrow resolver boundary.

