H07-028 design decision after canonical checkpoint palette audit:

I do **not** recommend automatic legacy reconciliation (Strategy A) for worlds generated by `main=4516387f...`. The checkpoint wrote no mod-version/provenance marker, and every physical signature is player-reproducible. Even exact deterministic candidate + full expected MAGMA/CALCITE/TUFF/BASALT footprint cannot prove that Volcanoes, rather than a player, created it; `MUD_POT` is even more ambiguous because its entire footprint is vanilla MUD.

Conservative release strategy should therefore be **B + C**:
- treat `4516387f...` geothermal terrain as an intermediate development snapshot with **no automatic metadata promotion**;
- provide a bounded preview/admin reconciliation path for loaded owner chunks only;
- preview recomputes the single deterministic candidate/profile and reports exact footprint evidence, existing source/deposit authority and ambiguity, but never reshapes terrain or force-loads neighbors;
- explicit admin confirmation may create/reconcile metadata through the same canonical source/deposit authority path, idempotently;
- MUD_POT and partially edited footprints remain explicit/manual only;
- source removal must not be silently undone by any legacy scanner because no automatic scanner exists.

This is the only strategy I can currently justify against H07-028's strict false-positive constraint without inventing provenance that the checkpoint never persisted. Final acceptance still needs an existing-world upgrade test plus preview/confirmation tests when runners are available.

